    {
      "id": "qtm-m3-variance-sd-c2",
      "heading": "The formulas: Method 1, Method 2 and SD",
      "explanation_md": "**Method 1 (definition):**\n\nσ² = V(X) = E[(X - μ)²] = Σ (x - μ)² P(x) (over all x)\n\nTake each value's distance from the mean, square it, weight it by its probability, add.\n\n**Method 2 (computational formula):**\n\n**σ² = V(X) = E(X²) - [E(X)]²**\n\n\"Mean of the squares minus the square of the mean.\" Usually faster.\n\n**Standard deviation:**\n\n**σ = SD(X) = √V(X)**",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [
        {
          "term": "Method 1 (variance)",
          "meaning": "σ² = V(X) = E[(X - μ)²] = Σ (x - μ)² P(x).",
          "source_ref": "qtm--module-3#41"
        },
        {
          "term": "Method 2 (computational formula)",
          "meaning": "σ² = V(X) = E(X²) - [E(X)]².",
          "source_ref": "qtm--module-3#41"
        },
        {
          "term": "SD(X)",
          "meaning": "σ = SD(X) = √V(X).",
          "source_ref": "qtm--module-3#41"
        }
      ],
      "exam_line": "V(X) = Σ (x - μ)² P(x) (Method 1) = E(X²) - [E(X)]² (Method 2); SD(X) = √V(X).",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
