      "id": "qtm-m3-variance-sd-c3",
      "heading": "Dialing switches: variance by Method 1",
      "explanation_md": "**Switch scenario:** x = number of dialing switches.\n\n| x | P(x) | xP(x) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 0.1 | 0 |\n| 1 | 0.2 | 0.2 |\n| 2 | 0.3 | 0.6 |\n| 3 | 0.2 | 0.6 |\n| 4 | 0.1 | 0.4 |\n| 5 | 0.1 | 0.5 |\n| Total | 1.00 | **2.3 = E(X)** |\n\n**Variance (Method 1)** with μ = 2.3:\n\nσ² = Σ (x - μ)² P(x)\n= (0 - 2.3)²(0.1) + (1 - 2.3)²(0.2) + (2 - 2.3)²(0.3) + (3 - 2.3)²(0.2) + (4 - 2.3)²(0.1) + (5 - 2.3)²(0.1)\n= **2.01**\n\n**Standard deviation:** σ = SD(X) = √V(X) = √2.01 ≈ **1.42** (the slide shows the formula; this number is worked out from it).",
