    {
      "id": "qtm-m3-variance-sd-c5",
      "heading": "Example 2: variance of the monthly profit",
      "explanation_md": "Back to monthly sales: items 5,000 to 9,000 with P(x) = 0.2, 0.3, 0.2, 0.2, 0.1; fixed cost **$8,000**; each item brings **$2**. **Profit = 2X - 8,000.** Find the variance of the profit using the Type 2 approach.\n\n**Step 1: E(X²)**\n\nE(X²) = (5,000)²(0.2) + (6,000)²(0.3) + (7,000)²(0.2) + (8,000)²(0.2) + (9,000)²(0.1) = **46,500,000**\n\n**Step 2: V(X)**, with E(X) = **6,700**:\n\nV(X) = E(X²) - [E(X)]² = 46,500,000 - (6,700)² = **1,610,000**\n\n**Step 3: variance of the profit.** The slide multiplies by the square of the multiplier 2 (it cites its equation 3-10):\n\n2²(1,610,000) = **6,440,000**\n\n**Step 4: standard deviation of the profit:** √6,440,000 = **2,537.72**\n\nNotice the fixed $8,000 does not appear in step 3: only the multiplier 2 matters, and it is squared.",
      "example_ids": [
        "qtm-ex-m3-profit-variance"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
