    {
      "id": "qtm-m3-variance-sd-c6",
      "heading": "Exercise: the oil well",
      "explanation_md": "An oil well investment has three outcomes:\n\n| x = outcome in $ | p(x) |\n|---|---|\n| -40,000 (no oil) | .25 |\n| 10,000 (some oil) | .7 |\n| 70,000 (much oil) | .05 |\n\nNo answers are printed on the slide, so here is the working with the deck's formulas.\n\n**Q1. Expected monetary outcome, E(X) = Σ x P(x):**\n\n(-40,000)(.25) + (10,000)(.7) + (70,000)(.05) = -10,000 + 7,000 + 3,500 = **$500**\n\n**Q2. Variance, using Method 2:**\n\nE(X²) = (40,000)²(.25) + (10,000)²(.7) + (70,000)²(.05) = 400,000,000 + 70,000,000 + 245,000,000 = 715,000,000\n\nV(X) = 715,000,000 - (500)² = 715,000,000 - 250,000 = **714,750,000**\n\nStandard deviation = √714,750,000 ≈ **26,734.81**\n\nA small positive expected outcome with a huge standard deviation: a risky investment.",
      "example_ids": [
        "qtm-ex-m3-oil-well"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Oil well: E(X) = -10,000 + 7,000 + 3,500 = $500; V(X) = 715,000,000 - 500² = 714,750,000.",
